# a32wifiadapter — push source, docs and evidence; rebuild the rest.
#
# KEPT deliberately (source of truth):
#   README.md, docs/, a32router/ (module source), pc/ (scripts+units),
#   audit/ (report + raw evidence), test/0*.log (engineering logs),
#   test/*.py (probe tools), test/btsnooz_hci.log (cited BT evidence).

# ---- Build artifacts (reproducible: see README Status section) ----
# Magisk zips are built from a32router/, e.g.:
#   (cd a32router && zip -qr ../a32router-vX.Y.Z.zip . \
#     -x 'state/*' 'a32router.log' '*.old' '__pycache__/*')
*.zip

# ---- Python bytecode ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# ---- Test-runner caches ----
.pytest_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# ---- Live daemon logs from manual runs (repo root only;
# ---- test/*.log are curated engineering history — KEEP those) ----
/*.log

# ---- Local runtime droppings our tooling may create ----
*.tmp
*.pid
*.leases
*.log.*
*.old
*.bak

# ---- Agent/harness session state (tool bookkeeping, not project) ----
.pi/

# ---- Editor / OS noise ----
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/
